                        "form_id": "f72d4b98-c6a6-49f0-89a0-a0dac78ffeb7",
                        "entry_id": "a896e714-c0d0-3c7b-920f-0cf546583e4a",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "post-vérité"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "368268ae-0ac4-3233-9ef5-997cb57fdc18",
                        "entry_id": "a896e714-c0d0-3c7b-920f-0cf546583e4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Situation dans laquelle l’objectivité et la véracité des faits ont moins d’influence sur la formation de l’opinion publique que le recours à des émotions, à des sentiments ou à des croyances."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57450ed8-a004-4ace-9caf-711efbd6513a",
                                "sense_id": "368268ae-0ac4-3233-9ef5-997cb57fdc18",
                                "text": "Maurizio Ferraris explique comment faire face à la postvérité qu’il décrit comme une atomisation de la vérité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5765f3-acd7-4a32-9e2c-f05c122f3015",
                                "sense_id": "368268ae-0ac4-3233-9ef5-997cb57fdc18",
                                "text": "Cet exemple pointe la complexité du phénomène des « fake news », de la postvérité ou de quel que soit le nom que l’on donne aujourd’hui au mensonge et à la propagande."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af43c557-1835-48ae-b055-f74a203e2d90",
                        "source_entry_id": "a896e714-c0d0-3c7b-920f-0cf546583e4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "368268ae-0ac4-3233-9ef5-997cb57fdc18",
                        "target_lang_word": "posttruth",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "posttruth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f64fc9b5-8978-3db3-b421-426cfe5852a1",
                                        "entry_id": "19d59d09-db81-3c60-a527-7423e7f97659",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of post-truth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c89617f7-f024-455f-b6c7-d17aa87d0aa5",
                                                "sense_id": "f64fc9b5-8978-3db3-b421-426cfe5852a1",
                                                "text": "Indeed, in what follows, we entertain several tenuous interpretations of the film, ones that display prominent aspects of postcolonial theory and perhaps even address some sort of posttruth in their microscopic readings but ones that, through excess essentially, mock such applications of postcolonial theory, as they question the warping power of theory in general."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7e2a404-52db-48f1-bc69-816d526c5180",
                                                "sense_id": "f64fc9b5-8978-3db3-b421-426cfe5852a1",
                                                "text": "Across multiple societies, we see a shift from regimes of truth (ROT) to “regimes of posttruth”(ROPT) characterized by proliferating “truth markets.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "posttruth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4d16d89-c31e-3bfc-9ee0-99fd97f84f18",
                                        "entry_id": "116dd259-6e7b-37b2-9baf-7ab3ad3d1656",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of post-truth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b3c3cae-f448-4d5f-8bba-1dd9d2a8df95",
                                                "sense_id": "a4d16d89-c31e-3bfc-9ee0-99fd97f84f18",
                                                "text": "Hartley uses the term 'posttruth society' to characterize a binary-oriented journalism in which 'reason and truth are not the guiding principles' but rather 'adversarial visions' that pit 'we' groups against 'they' groups (1992: 217)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4435813e-5e14-401a-ab8c-309a378db8fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "a896e714-c0d0-3c7b-920f-0cf546583e4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "368268ae-0ac4-3233-9ef5-997cb57fdc18",
                        "target_lang_word": "post-truth",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "post-truth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                        "entry_id": "7cb575ed-578e-3ec1-8331-f55de78a446c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Beyond or superseding the importance of truth; pertaining to an era or situation when truth is no longer significant, relevant, or expected; (usually derogatory) not caring about factual accuracy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76df74c8-c5fe-414b-bcc3-db442ccdc3fd",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "He is, he claims, post-God, post-reality, post-truth, post-meaning, post- history, post-world, post-Western […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd12c351-410b-47dd-848b-78f04f138562",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "Victims or exiles should not repeat any longer what everybody already knows in the new 'post-truth' world order – that they are among numerous contemporary victims of war crimes and military violence […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2a75d2b-19a5-4877-a3b0-be73c9892542",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "Clearly quite a lot of journalism is post-truth . . . More important, perhaps, is journalism's post-truth tendency . . . to make no propositions for which there is a possible 'true/false' response."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "636a627a-7526-4d7f-95ad-d45298e2e102",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "In the post-truth world, the people are saturated by a plurality of discourses that are struggling for the consent of the audience, the difference being that the explosion of messages that characterises modernity is no longer stamped with the 'authority' of their authors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc453c81-7817-4352-a559-d4628ca20471",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "In Christianity Today, columnist Charles Colson bemoaned our “post-truth society,” which produces liars such as Tawana Brawley, David Brock, and Stephen Ambrose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0e4b80e-259c-4d0c-a4d4-a95eb225f510",
                                                "sense_id": "0244f04a-d751-38a3-af17-fc424d6e2977",
                                                "text": "Avoiding a cacophony is a worthy objective, because Australia has managed to largely sidestep the post-truth hellscape the US has endured during the pandemic because politicians, by and large, have chosen to inhabit a universe of shared facts and common messages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "post-truth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91d80ae0-7cf2-34ea-8ffe-9c6199f8076f",
                                        "entry_id": "9b77a77c-2650-34c1-a515-a5d3a6495379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fact or state of being post-truth; a time period or situation in which facts have become less important than emotional persuasion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbb95a8b-fac1-49d9-a850-45d01e5494dc",
                                                "sense_id": "91d80ae0-7cf2-34ea-8ffe-9c6199f8076f",
                                                "text": "Post-truth has also been abetted by the evolution of the media."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
